Given a ring <MATH_0005> and an element <MATH_0006> there exists a unique\nring homomorphism <MATH_0007> which maps <MATH_0008> to <MATH_0009>.\nThus, using Lemma <REF_0001>, we see that\n<MATH_0010>\nThis does indeed\ngive an isomorphism <MATH_0011>.\nWhat is the ``universal family'' <MATH_0012>? To get it we have to\napply the identifications above to <MATH_0013>.\nClearly under the identifications above this gives\nthat\n<MATH_0014>\nas expected.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:685a2945412bb46af6ecc65a8a3f451f746fa34cfce9aef81349375d8c94760e", "unit_id": "inventory:schemes:01JH:example/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:575349c83a1f1de120034af803ccef805d8f1225691c71885f45a1ade5e00343", "hash": "sha256:575349c83a1f1de120034af803ccef805d8f1225691c71885f45a1ade5e00343", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 103678, "byte_start": 103112, "file": "schemes.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:e8e5798d2a1c7e1e4480975b1a91571fabe6c16df35f9c55e7dd0f96e78406ce", "line_end": 2907, "line_start": 2892}, "owner_tag": "01JJ", "parent_tag": "01JF", "requested_label": "schemes-lemma-glue-functors", "requested_tag": "01JJ", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01JF", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-glue-functors}", "MATH_0001": "$F$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$I$", "MATH_0004": "$F_i \\subset F$", "MATH_0005": "$F_i$", "MATH_0006": "$F_i \\subset F$", "MATH_0007": "$(F_i)_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$F$", "MATH_0009": "$F$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\item", "STRUCT_0009": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0010": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0011": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_ver